      "id": "00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000011",
      "title": "Welcome to Devot",
      "bodyMd": "This is your library. Everything you write stays on this device, in a database in the app's data folder, and nothing is sent anywhere. Delete this notebook whenever you like: it will not come back.\n\n## Organize\n\n- **Notebooks** hold notes and can nest. Make one with the _New Notebook_ button in the sidebar, and drag notebooks and notes to move them.\n- **Tags** go on any note from the command palette (⌘K). Click a tag in the sidebar to filter the list by it.\n- **Status** marks where a note stands: None ⌃⌘1, Active ⌃⌘2, On Hold ⌃⌘3, Completed ⌃⌘4, Dropped ⌃⌘5.\n- **Pin to Top** keeps a note at the top of its list (P in the note list).\n- **Templates** start a note from a note of your own: New Note from Template, ⌘T.\n- Deleted notes wait in the **Trash** (⌘⌫ in the note list) until you empty it.\n\n## Write\n\nEach note has four views: _Show Write Mode_, _Show Editor_, _Show Editor and Preview_ and _Show Preview_. Write Mode has its own round button and renders the note as you write, revealing the Markdown of the element under the caret. The editor shows all your Markdown with its syntax highlighted; the preview shows the result and scrolls along with the editor.\n\n| Do this                       | Press                                                                           |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| New note                      | ⌘N                                                                |\n| Bold, italic, strikethrough   | ⌘B, ⌘I, ⌘U        |\n| Inline code, code block       | ⌥⌘E, ⇧⌘C                                   |\n| Link                          | ⌥⌘K                                                             |\n| Headings 1 to 6               | ⌘1 to ⌥⌘6                              |\n| Bulleted, numbered, task list | ⇧⌘L, ⇧⌘O, ⇧⌘T |\n| Quote                         | ⌘'                                                            |\n\nType `/` at the start of a line for a menu of everything you can insert, and `[[` to link to another note by its title. Paste or drop an image to attach it to the note. See the **Markdown example** note in this notebook for every kind of Markdown Devot understands.\n\n## Find your way\n\n- **Command palette** ⌘K: every command, notes, notebooks and tags in one list.\n- **Find in the note** ⌘F, and replace ⌥⌘F.\n- **Search** the library ⇧⌘F, or all notes ⌥⇧⌘F. Searching understands words, phrases and filters such as notebook and tag names.\n- **Back and forward** between notes: ⌘[ and ⌘]. Next and previous note: ⇧⌘] and ⇧⌘[.\n- **Hide the sidebar** ⌘/, **Focus Mode** ⇧⌘D, and the text size ⌘= bigger, ⌘- smaller, ⌘0 back to normal.\n- **History** ⌥⌘Y lists the versions of a note and shows what changed between them.\n\n## Your data\n\n- Devot backs up the library every day and keeps the last seven backups (_Backups_ in the command palette).\n- The **Markdown Mirror** keeps a folder of plain `.md` files in step with your notes, if you choose one in the command palette.\n- Any note exports as Markdown, HTML or PDF from its menu, and a Markdown folder can be imported.\n- Notebooks are closed to AI tools until you switch _Allow AI Access_ on for a notebook.\n\nHave a look at the [Markdown example](devot://note/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000012) next.\n",
